course: dictionary
lesson: 1214
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word buffalo is a good example. It can be an animal, a city, or a name for another animal. «Lionesses do most of the hunting, often as a team, but males hunt too, especially big animals like buffalo.» Lions hunt buffalo, so here buffalo is an animal.
explain: Clues often sit close to the word. «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields in southern China for thousands of years.» Water tells you it is a kind of buffalo, and ploughs and rice fields tell you it is a working farm animal. Look at the words next to the one you do not know.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about first. If it talks about a place in New York State, or a spicy chicken dish, buffalo means the city. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: A buffalo is a large animal of the cattle family, with big curved horns.
fact: The African buffalo is one of the «Big Five» animals on safari.
fact: Water buffalo give milk, and «real mozzarella is buffalo milk».
fact: In North America, people often call the American bison a buffalo, though scientists say bison is the correct name.
fact: Buffalo is also a city in New York State, USA, and «buffalo wings» are spicy chicken named after it.
exercise: «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields.» What were water buffaloes doing here? | Swimming in the rice | Carrying children to school | *Pulling ploughs on a farm | Flying over the fields
exercise: «Lionesses hunt big animals like buffalo.» What kind of word is buffalo in this sentence? | A spicy chicken dish | A name for a river | A city in the USA | *An animal
exercise: Which is the scientists' correct name for the animal many people call a buffalo in North America? | African buffalo | Water buffalo | Yak | *Bison
test: «Buffalo wings» are spicy chicken. What does buffalo mean in this phrase? | *Named after the city of Buffalo | A water animal | A huge animal with horns | A type of bread
test: «A herd of buffalo grazed by the river.» What does herd mean here? | A kind of fence | A single animal | *A group of animals | A long walk
exam: «A buffalo stood in the mud, pulling a plough.» Which meaning fits best? | A spicy chicken dish | A name for a river | *An animal of the cattle family | A city in New York State
